! -- Warrant abstract --
! Land office Military Warrant No. 1155 for John Ritcheson 200A due unto John Ritcheson in consideration of his services for the War as Soldier in the Virginia Continental line ... Given ... 24th Day of June 1783 (No. 1 July 10th 1787) [Reverse] Doctr Benjamin Johnston will act pay jus + rect the plott
! Survey - Surveyed for John Hughes and William Roberts assee 1275 Acres of Land, Viz Hughes 1000 on part of a Military Wart No. 838 and Roberts 275 Acres on No. 1155 and part of 1059 on the West side of Pond River
! [Reverse side of survey] ... For value received I do hereby transfer convey and assign unto William Roberts his Heirs and assigns all my right title and claim to my part of the within platt and certificate of Survey and the Rigister of the Land office is hereby desired to Issue the grant accordingly  In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this 8 day of July 1794 - Jno Hughes (Seal)
! Washington County State Pennsylvania April 12th 1784 I John Richardson for value rec'd do assign + make over unto Benjamin Johnston his heirs and assigns a Land Warrant granted to me for my Services in the Virginia Continental Service for two hundred acres of Land dated 24 June 1783 No. 1155 and do hereby desire the same may be transfered and deeded in his or his heirs or assigns name Witness my hand + seal the day + year first above written - John Richardson (Seal), Witness [?]Ephrai Duiby
! We do hereby certify that the warants above mentioned were appraised + sold as part of the Estate of Ben Johnston dec'd of which John Harrison became the purchaser. April 30 1792 Will Johnston, G ? J Johnston, admsrs  -- I assign the above to William Roberts his Heirs or assigns for value rec'd April 30th 1792 - Jno Harrison
Rec 
Re 1275A BLFPR
